{"description":"Send a text message to one named device, or broadcast to every registered device, and display what arrives.\n\nEach message carries a client-generated ULID so redelivery is harmless, and both the sender's send time and the coordinator's receive time, because clock skew across the fleet is expected and neither timestamp alone can be trusted.\n\nOrdering is per conversation. A global total order across the tailnet is explicitly not provided and must not be assumed by anything built on this.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. A message from device A to device B, both online, is displayed on B.\n2. A broadcast from A is displayed on every other online device.\n3. Delivering the same ULID twice to a receiver produces one displayed message.\n4. Both timestamps are retained and both are visible to the user, so skew is legible rather than hidden.\n5. Works on a build compiled without the `voice` tag, on linux/amd64 and linux/arm64."}